+# ADR 0001: Document the sample's existing startup behavior
+
+## Background
+
+The only milestone in the development plan is missing README guidance for starting the sample, inspecting help, and configuring `APP_PORT`. There are no existing tasks or ADRs. `app.py` uses Python's standard library and prints the selected port before exiting.
+
+## Decision
+
+Create T001 as one documentation work unit. Document commands from the repository root using Python 3, help, default port 8080, and a per-command environment override. Describe the observed print-and-exit behavior. Keep the implementation unchanged. Retain command output and document checks in a new T001 run.
+
+## Alternatives
+
+- Add only a task proposal: this would leave the authorized milestone unfinished.
+- Expand the sample into a server: no such implementation change is in scope.
+- Create several tasks for the same README: the outputs and prerequisites are shared and fit one work unit.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The README can be verified against the local CLI. Local completion does not mean adoption into main or completion of a WCAG audit. A remote PR cannot be created in this evaluation because there is no remote and network/real PR operations are prohibited; the task retains that handoff explicitly.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run the default command with `APP_PORT` unset, the help command, and an override of 9090. Compare their exit codes and output with the README. Check local Markdown links, task/index correspondence, dependency facts, and whitespace. See [T001](../tasks/T001-startup-documentation.md) for the new run and results.
